  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 140 AM CDT Fri Aug 21 2026\n\nThrough the remainder of the forecast period, we will remain \ndominated by upper level northwest flow. This will continue to usher \nshortwaves through the area, which will help dampen the ridge that \nis forecast to set up over the Rockies. Although, this pattern is \nnot favorable for much moisture return. Thus, precipitation chances \nwill remain limited through this timeframe, with passing clouds and \nshifting winds being the main signs of the passing waves. \nTemperatures will remain seasonal and hover around 80 degrees, with \nlow humidity to make it quite pleasant. After Friday night, our \nprecipitation chances will be quite limited. Some global models \nskirt our south with precipitation chances from a passing system on \nMonday, and then more widespread PoPs midweek, albeit low. Overall, \nchances for precipitation with both of these systems generally fall \nbetween 20-40%.",
